<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
            http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
      The music frames on waves 02 and 03 take their final size (DESIGN §7.5).

      WAVE 02: A SQUARE. The cover is square, so the frame must be square too: then
      `contain` fills the tile entirely, and the blurred fill at the sides degenerates into a border
      of a couple of pixels. We compute from the board's real geometry, not "by eye":

        width(n)  = 33.7px * n + 4px * (n-1)      (40 columns on 1504px, gap 4)
        height(m) = 25.86px * m + 4px * (m-1)     (28 rows on 832px, gap 4)

      The gaps cancel out, and the square condition reduces to n/m = 0.792. Of the integer pairs
      7x9 is the closest (263x267, a 1.6% miss); the neighbouring 6x8 and 8x10 miss by 5% and 1.2%,
      but 7 columns also give EXACT centring under "Today" (13 columns, centre 21.5:
      it matches only with an odd span).

      Nine rows did not fit in the old place: the tile stands in the bottom band, and its bottom hits
      the edge of the grid. So "Today" gives up one row (15→14): the freed row 19
      becomes an air spacer, and the frame starts at row 20. The dominant tile loses 26 pixels
      of height: unnoticeable on the trail map, and the frame gets its proportion.

      ⚠️ The square is exact on the owner's screen (1536x864). The board's height is `calc(100vh - 32px)`,
      so on a screen of another height the rows change their step and the frame stretches slightly. There is
      no cure without leaving the proportional grid; the side fill covers exactly
      this difference.

      WAVE 03: one row lower. The Spotify plate lost its playlist row (the skin), and the height
      for it is no longer needed. Seven rows instead of eight is the owner's "signature touch": the plate is
      noticeably flatter than everything else on the board, and that is its mark.
    -->
    <changeSet id="0570-music-frames-final" author="danchuo">
        <sql><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme
SET layout = jsonb_set(
        jsonb_set(layout, '{tiles,music}', $J${"col": 19, "row": 20, "colSpan": 7, "rowSpan": 9}$J$::jsonb),
        '{tiles,today}',
        $J${"col": 16, "row": 5, "colSpan": 13, "rowSpan": 14}$J$::jsonb
    )
WHERE key = 'wave-02';

UPDATE theme
SET layout = jsonb_set(
        layout,
        '{tiles,music}',
        $J${"col": 16, "row": 8, "colSpan": 10, "rowSpan": 6}$J$::jsonb
    )
WHERE key = 'wave-03';
        ]]></sql>
        <rollback><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme
SET layout = jsonb_set(
        jsonb_set(layout, '{tiles,music}', $J${"col": 18, "row": 21, "colSpan": 9, "rowSpan": 8}$J$::jsonb),
        '{tiles,today}',
        $J${"col": 16, "row": 5, "colSpan": 13, "rowSpan": 15}$J$::jsonb
    )
WHERE key = 'wave-02';

UPDATE theme
SET layout = jsonb_set(
        layout,
        '{tiles,music}',
        $J${"col": 16, "row": 8, "colSpan": 10, "rowSpan": 7}$J$::jsonb
    )
WHERE key = 'wave-03';
        ]]></rollback>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
